            "plainText": "| Concept | Core Point |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Knowability | We know God truly but not totally — always by His gracious accommodation |\n| Creator–creature distinction | God alone is uncreated; our knowledge of Him is analogical and received |\n| Classical arguments | Pointers to God's existence; leave the unbeliever without excuse (Rom. 1:20) |\n| Aseity | God is self-existent and self-sufficient — He needs nothing, owes nothing, lacks nothing |\n| Revelation | General (creation/conscience) gives context; Special (Scripture/Christ) gives the gospel |"
