            "heading": "8. Summary",
            "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Theme</th><th>Core Point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Trinitarian prayer</td><td>To the Father, through the Son, by the Spirit — the full Trinitarian structure of Christian prayer</td></tr><tr><td>Love and community</td><td>God is eternally love <em>within</em> the Trinity; human community reflects and participates in this</td></tr><tr><td>Philippine context</td><td><em>Kapwa</em>, equality in difference, self-giving rather than self-seeking — all grounded Trinitarianly</td></tr><tr><td>Corporate worship</td><td>Genuinely Trinitarian worship addresses Father, mediates through Son, depends on the Spirit</td></tr><tr><td>Mission</td><td>The Gospel is a Trinitarian story — told rightly only with all three persons in view</td></tr><tr><td>Eternal joy</td><td>The Trinitarian life is not just doctrine but the eternal joy into which we are being drawn</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
            "plainText": "| Theme | Core Point |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Trinitarian prayer | To the Father, through the Son, by the Spirit — the full Trinitarian structure of Christian prayer |\n| Love and community | God is eternally love within the Trinity; human community reflects and participates in this |\n| Philippine context | Kapwa, equality in difference, self-giving rather than self-seeking — all grounded Trinitarianly |\n| Corporate worship | Genuinely Trinitarian worship addresses Father, mediates through Son, depends on the Spirit |\n| Mission | The Gospel is a Trinitarian story — told rightly only with all three persons in view |\n| Eternal joy | The Trinitarian life is not just doctrine but the eternal joy into which we are being drawn |"
