    "description": "What must a person do to be saved? This course takes students through the biblical drama of sin, grace, justification, and perseverance — grounding them in the Reformation's recovered gospel. Beginning with the depth of human ruin and ending with the certainty of final salvation, the course equips students to understand what they have been saved from, saved by, saved through, and saved for.",
