            "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Figure / Event</th><th>Core Significance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ignatius &amp; Polycarp</td><td>Apostolic connection; martyrdom as confession; early opposition to Docetism</td></tr><tr><td>Irenaeus</td><td>Defeat of Gnosticism; <em>regula fidei</em>; Scripture&#x27;s unity against Marcion</td></tr><tr><td>Athanasius</td><td><em>Contra mundum</em> — the Son is <em>homoousios</em>; Nicaea defended at great personal cost</td></tr><tr><td>Augustine</td><td>Original sin, bondage of will, prevenient grace — the soil of the Reformation</td></tr><tr><td>Arianism</td><td>A reduced Christ cannot save; precision matters</td></tr><tr><td>Pelagianism</td><td>Human self-improvement is always the default heresy</td></tr><tr><td>The creeds</td><td>Summaries of Scripture under pressure — not co-equal with it, but faithful to it</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
            "plainText": "| Figure / Event | Core Significance |\n|----------------|-------------------|\n| Ignatius & Polycarp | Apostolic connection; martyrdom as confession; early opposition to Docetism |\n| Irenaeus | Defeat of Gnosticism; regula fidei; Scripture's unity against Marcion |\n| Athanasius | Contra mundum — the Son is homoousios; Nicaea defended at great personal cost |\n| Augustine | Original sin, bondage of will, prevenient grace — the soil of the Reformation |\n| Arianism | A reduced Christ cannot save; precision matters |\n| Pelagianism | Human self-improvement is always the default heresy |\n| The creeds | Summaries of Scripture under pressure — not co-equal with it, but faithful to it |"
