            "heading": "7. Summary",
            "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Core Point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medieval church</td><td>Sacramental system; grace through the church; justification as infused process</td></tr><tr><td>Luther&#x27;s discovery</td><td>Righteousness of God as gift received by faith, not standard to achieve</td></tr><tr><td><em>Sola Scriptura</em></td><td>Scripture alone as final authority — above councils, popes, tradition</td></tr><tr><td><em>Sola Fide</em></td><td>Faith alone as the instrument of justification — not faith plus works</td></tr><tr><td><em>Sola Gratia</em></td><td>Grace alone — no human merit initiates or completes salvation</td></tr><tr><td><em>Solus Christus</em></td><td>Christ alone as mediator — no supplementary intercession permitted</td></tr><tr><td><em>Soli Deo Gloria</em></td><td>Glory to God alone — the end of all redemption</td></tr><tr><td>Calvin</td><td>Systematiser, pastoral theologian; election, church government, regulative principle</td></tr><tr><td>Philippines</td><td>Counter-Reformation context; Reformation truths are minority but biblical inheritance</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
            "plainText": "| Concept | Core Point |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Medieval church | Sacramental system; grace through the church; justification as infused process |\n| Luther's discovery | Righteousness of God as gift received by faith, not standard to achieve |\n| Sola Scriptura | Scripture alone as final authority — above councils, popes, tradition |\n| Sola Fide | Faith alone as the instrument of justification — not faith plus works |\n| Sola Gratia | Grace alone — no human merit initiates or completes salvation |\n| Solus Christus | Christ alone as mediator — no supplementary intercession permitted |\n| Soli Deo Gloria | Glory to God alone — the end of all redemption |\n| Calvin | Systematiser, pastoral theologian; election, church government, regulative principle |\n| Philippines | Counter-Reformation context; Reformation truths are minority but biblical inheritance |"
