            "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Core Point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Apologetics defined</td><td>A reasoned defense of the faith — clearing barriers so the gospel can be heard</td></tr><tr><td>1 Peter 3:15</td><td>The command: always ready; the manner: gentleness and respect</td></tr><tr><td>Worldview framework</td><td>Anderson: everyone has presuppositions; the question is which set is most coherent</td></tr><tr><td>Presuppositional approach</td><td>Challenge the unbeliever&#x27;s foundations, not just add evidence to a neutral observer</td></tr><tr><td>Bavinck&#x27;s observation</td><td>Remove God and you get not freedom but chaos; the vacuum fills with quasi-religions</td></tr><tr><td>Total depravity and apologetics</td><td>The problem is not insufficient evidence but suppression (Rom. 1:18)</td></tr><tr><td>Unanswered vs. unanswerable</td><td>Kruger: do not confuse &quot;I don&#x27;t have an answer yet&quot; with &quot;this has no answer&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Tone</td><td>Gentleness and respect are not optional — they are part of the command</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
            "plainText": "| Concept | Core Point |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Apologetics defined | A reasoned defense of the faith — clearing barriers so the gospel can be heard |\n| 1 Peter 3:15 | The command: always ready; the manner: gentleness and respect |\n| Worldview framework | Anderson: everyone has presuppositions; the question is which set is most coherent |\n| Presuppositional approach | Challenge the unbeliever's foundations, not just add evidence to a neutral observer |\n| Bavinck's observation | Remove God and you get not freedom but chaos; the vacuum fills with quasi-religions |\n| Total depravity and apologetics | The problem is not insufficient evidence but suppression (Rom. 1:18) |\n| Unanswered vs. unanswerable | Kruger: do not confuse \"I don't have an answer yet\" with \"this has no answer\" |\n| Tone | Gentleness and respect are not optional — they are part of the command |"
